  "title": "The Wish That Needed a Verb",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "fantasy and science fiction",
  "premise": "A figure receives one wish token and asks for BETTER, causing a magical helper to improve random nearby objects while missing the real need. The figure replaces the vague word with HELP ME REACH THAT SHELF, and the helper grows one small stable-looking fantasy step so the figure can retrieve a cherished drawing.",
  "hook": "Better what? The wish is improvising.",
  "visible_action": "Objects gain absurd sparkles and extra drawers; wish text changes into a concrete request; one step appears; drawing is reached.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A concrete goal is easier to act on than a vague improvement.",
